{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A lamb, tamim.</b> So that the Jew could not take a blemished one to evade the Egyptian and say, 'this is not fit for you, and you should not be particular about it, since it is blemished, female, and old.' Therefore it says <b>tamim, a male, a year old</b> — even though they offer it for their worship, even so there is no reason to fear them. When you fear, they have no ability — their fear of you persists while you are in the city, all the more so when you go out of the city outside, they will not be able to bring you back." "<b>A year old.</b> In its first year. And the proof is from the princes, as it is written 'one lamb בן שנתו,' and at the end it is written 'twelve lambs בני שנה.' [From the sheep and from the goats, or from the goats.]"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The text appears slightly garbled; כשתיראו is rendered 'when you fear' hyper-literally, and the sentence שאין יכולת בידם להציל יראתם מכם 'they have no ability to save — their fear of you' is translated as found despite its awkward syntax."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:07.015041757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}